# Changelog

All notable changes to TripPlanner are documented here.

## [1.0.0] — 2026-06-08

### 🚀 Initial Release

#### Authentication
- Email/password registration and login with JWT
- Google OAuth2 single sign-on
- Role-based access control: USER, ADMIN, SUPER_ADMIN
- Change password from profile

#### Explore & Packages
- Browse predefined travel packages (Varanasi, Goa, Leh-Ladakh, Sikkim, etc.)
- Filter by category (Adventure, Relaxation, Luxury, Budget, Family, Spiritual)
- Filter by budget range, duration, season, transport mode
- Category and duration badges on package cards
- Dynamic pricing based on number of travelers

#### Payments & Bookings
- Razorpay payment gateway integration
- HMAC-SHA256 payment signature verification
- Booking history with status (CONFIRMED / CANCELLED)
- Cancel booking feature

#### My Trips (Custom Planning)
- Create personal trips with full metadata
- Invite members by email
- Trip lifecycle management (PLANNING → ONGOING → COMPLETED)

#### Expense Splitting
- Add expenses with description, amount, and category
- Equal split across selected participants
- Per-member balance view (Balances tab)
- Simplified transaction algorithm for debt settlement (Settle Up tab)
- Mark individual settlements as settled

#### Admin Panel
- Real-time dashboard: users, revenue, bookings, active packages
- Platform Monthly Revenue chart
- Bookings by Travel Category donut chart
- Add/Manage packages and predefined trips
- View all users and bookings

#### Infrastructure
- Spring Boot 3 backend on Azure App Service (Docker)
- React frontend on Vercel CDN
- Azure Database for MySQL Flexible Server
- Multi-stage Docker build
- Swagger UI API documentation
